window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b276-a2b2e3f6a8221964.json"]={sha256:"a2b2e3f6a8221964535f461eaf394e118a4ec996b98c1ca30fb721d8df91610c",value:{"id":"b276","title":"河岸生態護岸","titleEn":"Bioengineered riverbank protection","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"由趾部沖刷、木構浮力到根系補強與季節存活，逐一拆開生態護岸的承載機制。課程要求先辨認河道變遷與植物適生條件，再安排材料、施工窗口與後續監測，以對照組觀察功能是否形成，而不把綠色外觀當成安全證明。","summaryEn":"Separate the load paths of toe protection, buoyant wood, root reinforcement and seasonal plant establishment. Identify channel adjustment and vegetation suitability before selecting materials, construction windows and monitoring. Use comparison sites to examine whether the intended functions actually develop instead of treating a green bank as evidence of structural performance.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-river","architectureNodes":[["河岸剪力的尺度","Scales of bank shear"],["根系補強的有效面積","Effective area in root reinforcement"],["岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量","Toe embedment and erosion allowance"],["纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋","Mat overlap and effective coverage"],["對照監測的生態成效","Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-river","labels":["河岸剪力的尺度","根系補強的有效面積","岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量","纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋","對照監測的生態成效"],"labelsEn":["Scales of bank shear","Effective area in root reinforcement","Toe embedment and erosion allowance","Mat overlap and effective coverage","Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"本課先用「河岸剪力的尺度」建立原創假想基準，再以「植生莖叢的阻力」檢查另一個控制機制。第一組輸入及結果為 rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa；第二組為 rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N。學員需在同一張工作表分列量綱、時間、位置與適用範圍，先核對守恆，再解釋為何兩個得數不能互相代替。最後以第三單元提出的量測設計驗證假設，並將超出模型能力的水理、生態或治理問題列為待研究項目；這些示例並非所列案例的現場實測。敏感度重算：固定 rho=1000 kg/m3、g=9.81 m/s2 與 S=0.003 無因次，只將 R 從 0.8 m 增至 0.88 m，tau=25.8984 Pa，相較 23.544 Pa 增加一成。這仍是河段平均，不能當外彎局部最大值。","textEn":"Begin with an original hypothetical baseline for Scales of bank shear and examine another controlling mechanism through Drag on vegetation stems. The first inputs and result are rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa; the second are rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N. Keep dimensions, time, location and validity conditions in separate columns of the same working sheet. Check conservation before explaining why the two numerical results cannot substitute for one another. Use the third unit measurement design to test assumptions and identify hydraulic, ecological or governance questions that exceed the model. These examples are not field observations from the named reference cases. Sensitivity recalculation: Keep rho=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2 and dimensionless S=0.003 fixed, changing only R from 0.8 m to 0.88 m. The stress becomes 25.8984 Pa, ten percent above 23.544 Pa. It remains a reach average rather than the outer-bank local maximum.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b276-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「河岸剪力的尺度」與「植生莖叢的阻力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Scales of bank shear\" and \"Drag on vegetation stems\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b276-v15-01","title":"河岸剪力的尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Scales of bank shear: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「河岸剪力的尺度」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Scales of bank shear” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"河岸植生先面對水流造成的剪力與局部紊流，再由莖葉、根系及土體共同承受。斷面平均水力半徑乘以能坡只能估算河段平均床面剪力，彎道外岸、橋墩附近與淹沒植物間可能有完全不同的局部荷載。選工法前應把深槽、主流線和沖刷痕跡畫在同一張圖，辨認保護對象是表土、岸趾或整個滑動體，才決定平均量是否足以篩選材料。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「河岸剪力的尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Vegetation encounters flow shear and turbulence before stems, roots and soil share the resulting loads. Hydraulic radius and energy slope give a reach averaged boundary stress, while bends, obstructions and submerged plants can produce very different local loads. Map the thalweg, main current and erosion traces together. Identify whether protection targets surface soil, the toe or an entire sliding mass before deciding whether an average stress can screen a treatment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Scales of bank shear” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「河段平均剪力就是每一處岸坡承受的最大剪力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Reach average shear is the maximum stress at every bank location\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「河岸剪力的尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Scales of bank shear”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-01-k1","title":"河岸剪力的尺度","titleEn":"Scales of bank shear","text":"河岸植生先面對水流造成的剪力與局部紊流，再由莖葉、根系及土體共同承受。斷面平均水力半徑乘以能坡只能估算河段平均床面剪力，彎道外岸、橋墩附近與淹沒植物間可能有完全不同的局部荷載。","textEn":"Vegetation encounters flow shear and turbulence before stems, roots and soil share the resulting loads. Hydraulic radius and energy slope give a reach averaged boundary stress, while bends, obstructions and submerged plants can produce very different local loads.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：河段平均剪力就是每一處岸坡承受的最大剪力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Reach average shear is the maximum stress at every bank location Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「河岸剪力的尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Scales of bank shear\" is correct?","options":["河段平均剪力就是每一處岸坡承受的最大剪力","河岸植生先面對水流造成的剪力與局部紊流，再由莖葉、根系及土體共同承受。","種植面積可以直接代替所有莖葉的迎流投影面積"],"optionsEn":["Reach average shear is the maximum stress at every bank location","Vegetation encounters flow shear and turbulence before stems, roots and soil share the resulting loads.","Planted ground area directly equals the frontal area of all stems"],"answer":1,"explanation":"河岸植生先面對水流造成的剪力與局部紊流，再由莖葉、根系及土體共同承受。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Vegetation encounters flow shear and turbulence before stems, roots and soil share the resulting loads. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b276-v15-02","title":"河岸剪力的尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Scales of bank shear: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「河岸剪力的尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Scales of bank shear” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa。適用邊界：假設定常近均勻流，結果是平均邊界剪力，不是外彎岸坡最大剪力或植物耐受值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa. Applicable boundary: Assumes steady approximately uniform flow; the result is average boundary stress, not maximum outer-bank stress or plant resistance. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在同一水位下量測斷面與水面坡度，並以多點流速確認主流位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Survey cross sections and water surface slope at the same stage, and locate the current with multiple velocity measurements.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa。適用邊界：假設定常近均勻流，結果是平均邊界剪力，不是外彎岸坡最大剪力或植物耐受值。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa. Applicable boundary: Assumes steady approximately uniform flow; the result is average boundary stress, not maximum outer-bank stress or plant resistance.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「河岸剪力的尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Scales of bank shear\", which statement holds?","options":["木構的淨浮力除以錨點數就是每支錨具唯一荷載","原始植株存活百分比就是護岸抗剪強度保留百分比","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa。"],"optionsEn":["Net buoyancy divided by anchor count is the only load on each anchor","The surviving percentage of original plants equals the retained percentage of bank shear strength","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b276-v15-03","title":"河岸剪力的尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Scales of bank shear: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「河岸剪力的尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Scales of bank shear” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在同一水位下量測斷面與水面坡度，並以多點流速確認主流位置。分別記錄裸岸、草叢與岸趾附近的沖刷，若局部集中而平均剪力不高，應增加局部水理分析，不能只提高一個平均係數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Survey cross sections and water surface slope at the same stage, and locate the current with multiple velocity measurements. Record erosion near bare soil, vegetation and the toe separately. Concentrated erosion despite modest average stress requires local hydraulic investigation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：改以能坡增加一半重算平均剪力，再繪製兩個具有相同平均值但主流位置不同的斷面，說明哪一種情況需要增加岸趾量測，並列出判讀依據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase energy slope by half and recompute average shear. Sketch two sections with equal averages but different current positions, then explain which requires additional toe measurements and what observations would justify that decision.","failure":"注意干擾：彎道近岸高速帶可能掏空根區，使表面完整的植生毯失去支承。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A near-bank jet can undermine roots while the surface mat still appears intact. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在同一水位下量測斷面與水面坡度，並以多點流速確認主流位置。分別記錄裸岸、草叢與岸趾附近的沖刷，若局部集中而平均剪力不高，應增加局部水理分析，不能只提高一個平均係數。","textEn":"Survey cross sections and water surface slope at the same stage, and locate the current with multiple velocity measurements. Record erosion near bare soil, vegetation and the toe separately. Concentrated erosion despite modest average stress requires local hydraulic investigation.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"改以能坡增加一半重算平均剪力，再繪製兩個具有相同平均值但主流位置不同的斷面，說明哪一種情況需要增加岸趾量測，並列出判讀依據。","textEn":"Increase energy slope by half and recompute average shear. Sketch two sections with equal averages but different current positions, then explain which requires additional toe measurements and what observations would justify that decision.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「河岸剪力的尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Scales of bank shear\"?","options":["在同一水位下量測斷面與水面坡度，並以多點流速確認主流位置。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","岸面已經乾燥就代表深處孔隙水壓已完全消散"],"optionsEn":["Survey cross sections and water surface slope at the same stage, and locate the current with multiple velocity measurements.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A dry bank surface proves that deeper pore water pressure has completely dissipated"],"answer":0,"explanation":"在同一水位下量測斷面與水面坡度，並以多點流速確認主流位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Survey cross sections and water surface slope at the same stage, and locate the current with multiple velocity measurements. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b276-v15-04","title":"河岸剪力的尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Scales of bank shear: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「河岸剪力的尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Scales of bank shear” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"彎道近岸高速帶可能掏空根區，使表面完整的植生毯失去支承。診斷須追查水下岸趾與局部流向，而非先把植株死亡判成養護不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A near-bank jet can undermine roots while the surface mat still appears intact. Investigate the submerged toe and current direction before attributing plant loss to poor maintenance alone. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：選工法前應把深槽、主流線和沖刷痕跡畫在同一張圖，辨認保護對象是表土、岸趾或整個滑動體，才決定平均量是否足以篩選材料。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Identify whether protection targets surface soil, the toe or an entire sliding mass before deciding whether an average stress can screen a treatment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「河段平均剪力就是每一處岸坡承受的最大剪力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reach average shear is the maximum stress at every bank location\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"彎道近岸高速帶可能掏空根區，使表面完整的植生毯失去支承。診斷須追查水下岸趾與局部流向，而非先把植株死亡判成養護不足。","textEn":"A near-bank jet can undermine roots while the surface mat still appears intact. Investigate the submerged toe and current direction before attributing plant loss to poor maintenance alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「河岸剪力的尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Scales of bank shear\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","彎道近岸高速帶可能掏空根區，使表面完整的植生毯失去支承。","種植面積可以直接代替所有莖葉的迎流投影面積"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A near-bank jet can undermine roots while the surface mat still appears intact.","Planted ground area directly equals the frontal area of all stems"],"answer":1,"explanation":"彎道近岸高速帶可能掏空根區，使表面完整的植生毯失去支承。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A near-bank jet can undermine roots while the surface mat still appears intact. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b276-v15-05","title":"植生莖叢的阻力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Drag on vegetation stems: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「植生莖叢的阻力」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Drag on vegetation stems” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"植物在水中既增加粗糙度，也把水流動量轉成莖幹與根盤的荷載。迎流面積不是種植面積，而是投影在垂直流向平面的有效面積；柔軟植株彎伏後，面積與阻力係數會隨流速改變。群生植物還會彼此遮蔽或集中水流，因此單株試驗不能簡單乘株數。設計時應區分柔性變形、折斷和連根拔起三條失效路徑，並保留季節葉量不同的工況。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「植生莖叢的阻力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Vegetation adds roughness while transferring flow momentum into stems and roots. Frontal area is projected perpendicular to the current, not planted ground area. Flexible plants reconfigure, changing both area and drag coefficient as velocity increases. Neighbouring stems can shelter one another or concentrate flow, so multiplying an isolated plant test by stem count is unreliable. Distinguish bending, stem breakage and root pullout, and retain seasonal changes in foliage as separate loading conditions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drag on vegetation stems” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N.","failure":"常見誤解：「種植面積可以直接代替所有莖葉的迎流投影面積」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Planted ground area directly equals the frontal area of all stems\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「植生莖叢的阻力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drag on vegetation stems”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-05-k1","title":"植生莖叢的阻力","titleEn":"Drag on vegetation stems","text":"植物在水中既增加粗糙度，也把水流動量轉成莖幹與根盤的荷載。迎流面積不是種植面積，而是投影在垂直流向平面的有效面積；柔軟植株彎伏後，面積與阻力係數會隨流速改變。","textEn":"Vegetation adds roughness while transferring flow momentum into stems and roots. Frontal area is projected perpendicular to the current, not planted ground area.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：種植面積可以直接代替所有莖葉的迎流投影面積 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Planted ground area directly equals the frontal area of all stems Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「植生莖叢的阻力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Drag on vegetation stems\" is correct?","options":["種植面積可以直接代替所有莖葉的迎流投影面積","表層根系密度可直接代表任何深度滑動面的補強能力","植物在水中既增加粗糙度，也把水流動量轉成莖幹與根盤的荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Planted ground area directly equals the frontal area of all stems","Surface root density directly represents reinforcement on a failure plane at any depth","Vegetation adds roughness while transferring flow momentum into stems and roots."],"answer":2,"explanation":"植物在水中既增加粗糙度，也把水流動量轉成莖幹與根盤的荷載。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Vegetation adds roughness while transferring flow momentum into stems and roots. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b276-v15-06","title":"植生莖叢的阻力：定量估算","titleEn":"Drag on vegetation stems: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「植生莖叢的阻力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Drag on vegetation stems” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N。適用邊界：固定投影面積與阻力係數的準定常示例，未模擬彎伏、波動或群生效應。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N. Applicable boundary: A quasi-steady example with fixed projected area and drag coefficient, excluding reconfiguration, fluctuations and group effects. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以可量測拉力的小型枝條模型比較直立與彎伏狀態，逐級提高流速並拍攝迎流面積。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure force on a small branch model in upright and bent states while increasing velocity gradually.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N。適用邊界：固定投影面積與阻力係數的準定常示例，未模擬彎伏、波動或群生效應。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N. Applicable boundary: A quasi-steady example with fixed projected area and drag coefficient, excluding reconfiguration, fluctuations and group effects.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「植生莖叢的阻力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Drag on vegetation stems\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N。","剩餘埋深為正就代表護岸在所有洪水下都穩定","採購總面積等於完工後不重疊的有效覆蓋面積"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3.","Any positive remaining embedment proves stability under every flood","Purchased material area equals the effective nonoverlapping area after installation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b276-v15-07","title":"植生莖叢的阻力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Drag on vegetation stems: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「植生莖叢的阻力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Drag on vegetation stems” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以可量測拉力的小型枝條模型比較直立與彎伏狀態，逐級提高流速並拍攝迎流面積。把力除以速度平方後查看是否仍接近常數，若偏離便追查形狀改變，勿先當成儀器漂移。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure force on a small branch model in upright and bent states while increasing velocity gradually. Photograph the projected area. Examine force divided by velocity squared; changes may indicate reconfiguration rather than unexplained electronic sensor drift. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將流速增加百分之二十五並保持面積不變重算，再提出一個彎伏後面積縮小的對照案例，說明為何兩者的阻力增幅不同，以及所需影像資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase velocity by twenty five percent at fixed area, then construct a comparison with reduced area after bending. Explain the different force changes and identify the imagery needed to distinguish these cases.","failure":"注意干擾：洪水夾帶雜物會擴大有效迎流面積，使原先按清潔枝條估算的根部荷載偏低。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Debris can enlarge frontal area and make clean-stem calculations underestimate root loading. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以可量測拉力的小型枝條模型比較直立與彎伏狀態，逐級提高流速並拍攝迎流面積。把力除以速度平方後查看是否仍接近常數，若偏離便追查形狀改變，勿先當成儀器漂移。","textEn":"Measure force on a small branch model in upright and bent states while increasing velocity gradually. Photograph the projected area. Examine force divided by velocity squared; changes may indicate reconfiguration rather than unexplained electronic sensor drift.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將流速增加百分之二十五並保持面積不變重算，再提出一個彎伏後面積縮小的對照案例，說明為何兩者的阻力增幅不同，以及所需影像資料。","textEn":"Increase velocity by twenty five percent at fixed area, then construct a comparison with reduced area after bending. Explain the different force changes and identify the imagery needed to distinguish these cases.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「植生莖叢的阻力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Drag on vegetation stems\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以可量測拉力的小型枝條模型比較直立與彎伏狀態，逐級提高流速並拍攝迎流面積。","下游濃度下降就足以證明護岸永久移除了同等比例泥砂"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Measure force on a small branch model in upright and bent states while increasing velocity gradually.","Lower downstream concentration alone proves permanent removal of the same sediment fraction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以可量測拉力的小型枝條模型比較直立與彎伏狀態，逐級提高流速並拍攝迎流面積。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure force on a small branch model in upright and bent states while increasing velocity gradually. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b276-v15-08","title":"植生莖叢的阻力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Drag on vegetation stems: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「植生莖叢的阻力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Drag on vegetation stems” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"洪水夾帶雜物會擴大有效迎流面積，使原先按清潔枝條估算的根部荷載偏低。若只清點折枝而未查根盤位移，會漏掉尚未倒伏的損傷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Debris can enlarge frontal area and make clean-stem calculations underestimate root loading. Counting broken branches without checking root plate movement can miss damage in plants that remain standing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：設計時應區分柔性變形、折斷和連根拔起三條失效路徑，並保留季節葉量不同的工況。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Distinguish bending, stem breakage and root pullout, and retain seasonal changes in foliage as separate loading conditions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「種植面積可以直接代替所有莖葉的迎流投影面積」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Planted ground area directly equals the frontal area of all stems\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"洪水夾帶雜物會擴大有效迎流面積，使原先按清潔枝條估算的根部荷載偏低。若只清點折枝而未查根盤位移，會漏掉尚未倒伏的損傷。","textEn":"Debris can enlarge frontal area and make clean-stem calculations underestimate root loading. Counting broken branches without checking root plate movement can miss damage in plants that remain standing.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「植生莖叢的阻力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Drag on vegetation stems\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","表層根系密度可直接代表任何深度滑動面的補強能力","洪水夾帶雜物會擴大有效迎流面積，使原先按清潔枝條估算的根部荷載偏低。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Surface root density directly represents reinforcement on a failure plane at any depth","Debris can enlarge frontal area and make clean-stem calculations underestimate root loading."],"answer":2,"explanation":"洪水夾帶雜物會擴大有效迎流面積，使原先按清潔枝條估算的根部荷載偏低。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Debris can enlarge frontal area and make clean-stem calculations underestimate root loading. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b276-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「根系補強的有效面積」與「木構護岸的浮力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Effective area in root reinforcement\" and \"Buoyancy of wood revetments\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b276-v15-09","title":"根系補強的有效面積：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Effective area in root reinforcement: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「根系補強的有效面積」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective area in root reinforcement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"根系穿越潛在剪動面時可提供拉力，但這個貢獻取決於根徑、方向、錨定長度與含水狀態。把根拉力除以土體剪動面積只能得到等效的附加抗剪應力，不能當成整體土壤永久增加的黏聚力。部分根會先滑出或腐朽，另一些根尚未受力，因此同步動員的有效拉力必須由試驗支持。模型應清楚標示剪動面位置，避免把表層密根區的數據套到較深的滑動面。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「根系補強的有效面積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Roots crossing a potential shear surface can mobilize tension, depending on diameter, orientation, anchorage and moisture. Dividing effective root force by soil shear area gives an equivalent stress contribution, not a permanent increase in intrinsic soil cohesion. Some roots pull out or decay before others engage, so simultaneous mobilization requires evidence. Locate the assumed shear surface explicitly, rather than transferring measurements from a shallow dense root layer to a deeper failure plane. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective area in root reinforcement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「表層根系密度可直接代表任何深度滑動面的補強能力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Surface root density directly represents reinforcement on a failure plane at any depth\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「根系補強的有效面積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective area in root reinforcement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-09-k1","title":"根系補強的有效面積","titleEn":"Effective area in root reinforcement","text":"根系穿越潛在剪動面時可提供拉力，但這個貢獻取決於根徑、方向、錨定長度與含水狀態。把根拉力除以土體剪動面積只能得到等效的附加抗剪應力，不能當成整體土壤永久增加的黏聚力。","textEn":"Roots crossing a potential shear surface can mobilize tension, depending on diameter, orientation, anchorage and moisture. Dividing effective root force by soil shear area gives an equivalent stress contribution, not a permanent increase in intrinsic soil cohesion.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：表層根系密度可直接代表任何深度滑動面的補強能力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Surface root density directly represents reinforcement on a failure plane at any depth Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「根系補強的有效面積」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Effective area in root reinforcement\" is correct?","options":["根系穿越潛在剪動面時可提供拉力，但這個貢獻取決於根徑、方向、錨定長度與含水狀態。","表層根系密度可直接代表任何深度滑動面的補強能力","木構的淨浮力除以錨點數就是每支錨具唯一荷載"],"optionsEn":["Roots crossing a potential shear surface can mobilize tension, depending on diameter, orientation, anchorage and moisture.","Surface root density directly represents reinforcement on a failure plane at any depth","Net buoyancy divided by anchor count is the only load on each anchor"],"answer":0,"explanation":"根系穿越潛在剪動面時可提供拉力，但這個貢獻取決於根徑、方向、錨定長度與含水狀態。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Roots crossing a potential shear surface can mobilize tension, depending on diameter, orientation, anchorage and moisture. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b276-v15-10","title":"根系補強的有效面積：定量估算","titleEn":"Effective area in root reinforcement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「根系補強的有效面積」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective area in root reinforcement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa。適用邊界：有效拉力已假設包含方向與動員折減，僅代表指定剪面之附加應力。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa. Applicable boundary: Effective tension already includes assumed orientation and mobilization reductions; the result applies only to the specified shear surface. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對不同根徑做拉拔試驗，同時記錄斷裂或滑出模式，再量測剪動面上的根截面分布。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Test pullout across root diameters and record breakage versus slippage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa。適用邊界：有效拉力已假設包含方向與動員折減，僅代表指定剪面之附加應力。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa. Applicable boundary: Effective tension already includes assumed orientation and mobilization reductions; the result applies only to the specified shear surface.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「根系補強的有效面積」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Effective area in root reinforcement\", which statement holds?","options":["原始植株存活百分比就是護岸抗剪強度保留百分比","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa。","岸面已經乾燥就代表深處孔隙水壓已完全消散"],"optionsEn":["The surviving percentage of original plants equals the retained percentage of bank shear strength","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa.","A dry bank surface proves that deeper pore water pressure has completely dissipated"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b276-v15-11","title":"根系補強的有效面積：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Effective area in root reinforcement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「根系補強的有效面積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective area in root reinforcement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對不同根徑做拉拔試驗，同時記錄斷裂或滑出模式，再量測剪動面上的根截面分布。將單根強度與整體土樣剪切結果交叉比較，確認是否真的能同時動員，並保存含水率與植物生長期。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Test pullout across root diameters and record breakage versus slippage. Map roots across the proposed shear plane. Compare individual strength with rooted soil shear tests to assess simultaneous mobilization, retaining measured soil moisture and seasonal growth stage records. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將有效拉力降低四分之一重算，並畫出穿根與不穿根的兩個滑面。為每個滑面列出必須取得的試驗資料，說明等效應力何時應取零。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reduce effective tension by one quarter and recalculate. Draw failure planes crossing and bypassing roots, list the necessary evidence for each, and explain when the equivalent root contribution must be set to zero.","failure":"注意干擾：若實際滑動面位於根層下方，即使表層根系茂密也可能整塊滑落。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A slide beneath the root zone can remove a densely vegetated surface as one block. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對不同根徑做拉拔試驗，同時記錄斷裂或滑出模式，再量測剪動面上的根截面分布。將單根強度與整體土樣剪切結果交叉比較，確認是否真的能同時動員，並保存含水率與植物生長期。","textEn":"Test pullout across root diameters and record breakage versus slippage. Map roots across the proposed shear plane. Compare individual strength with rooted soil shear tests to assess simultaneous mobilization, retaining measured soil moisture and seasonal growth stage records.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將有效拉力降低四分之一重算，並畫出穿根與不穿根的兩個滑面。為每個滑面列出必須取得的試驗資料，說明等效應力何時應取零。","textEn":"Reduce effective tension by one quarter and recalculate. Draw failure planes crossing and bypassing roots, list the necessary evidence for each, and explain when the equivalent root contribution must be set to zero.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「根系補強的有效面積」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Effective area in root reinforcement\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","處理區植被增加的全部百分點都必然由護岸工程造成","對不同根徑做拉拔試驗，同時記錄斷裂或滑出模式，再量測剪動面上的根截面分布。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Every percentage point of vegetation gain in the treated reach must be caused by the works","Test pullout across root diameters and record breakage versus slippage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對不同根徑做拉拔試驗，同時記錄斷裂或滑出模式，再量測剪動面上的根截面分布。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Test pullout across root diameters and record breakage versus slippage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b276-v15-12","title":"根系補強的有效面積：失效診斷","titleEn":"Effective area in root reinforcement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「根系補強的有效面積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective area in root reinforcement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若實際滑動面位於根層下方，即使表層根系茂密也可能整塊滑落。應先查滑面深度與排水條件，而不是繼續增加表層播種密度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A slide beneath the root zone can remove a densely vegetated surface as one block. Investigate slip depth and drainage before prescribing more seed or greater surface planting density. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：模型應清楚標示剪動面位置，避免把表層密根區的數據套到較深的滑動面。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Locate the assumed shear surface explicitly, rather than transferring measurements from a shallow dense root layer to a deeper failure plane.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「表層根系密度可直接代表任何深度滑動面的補強能力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Surface root density directly represents reinforcement on a failure plane at any depth\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若實際滑動面位於根層下方，即使表層根系茂密也可能整塊滑落。應先查滑面深度與排水條件，而不是繼續增加表層播種密度。","textEn":"A slide beneath the root zone can remove a densely vegetated surface as one block. Investigate slip depth and drainage before prescribing more seed or greater surface planting density.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「根系補強的有效面積」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Effective area in root reinforcement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若實際滑動面位於根層下方，即使表層根系茂密也可能整塊滑落。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","木構的淨浮力除以錨點數就是每支錨具唯一荷載"],"optionsEn":["A slide beneath the root zone can remove a densely vegetated surface as one block.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Net buoyancy divided by anchor count is the only load on each anchor"],"answer":0,"explanation":"若實際滑動面位於根層下方，即使表層根系茂密也可能整塊滑落。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A slide beneath the root zone can remove a densely vegetated surface as one block. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b276-v15-13","title":"木構護岸的浮力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Buoyancy of wood revetments: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「木構護岸的浮力」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Buoyancy of wood revetments” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"河岸枯木或根盤可提供粗糙棲地，也可能在洪水中浮起。木材自重與排水體積必須用同一含水狀態比較，部分浸水時不能使用完整體積計算浮力。淨上浮力只是錨定設計的一個分量，水流拖曳、撞擊與繞支點轉動可能控制接頭。木構隨浸泡吸水與腐朽改變密度，因此檢查不能只依新材出廠重量，還需辨認失去土體包覆後的受力路徑。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「木構護岸的浮力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Wood and rootwads create rough habitat but may lift during floods. Compare weight and displaced volume at a consistent moisture state, and use submerged volume for partial immersion. Net uplift is only one anchorage load; drag, impact and rotation about supports may govern connections. Density changes through saturation and decay. Inspection therefore needs the evolving load path after surrounding soil erodes, rather than relying solely on the weight of freshly supplied timber. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Buoyancy of wood revetments” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhow=1000 kg/m3; rhol=600 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=0.8 m3; Fu=(rhow-rhol)*g*V=3139.2 N。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhow=1000 kg/m3; rhol=600 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=0.8 m3; Fu=(rhow-rhol)*g*V=3139.2 N.","failure":"常見誤解：「木構的淨浮力除以錨點數就是每支錨具唯一荷載」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Net buoyancy divided by anchor count is the only load on each anchor\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「木構護岸的浮力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Buoyancy of wood revetments”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-13-k1","title":"木構護岸的浮力","titleEn":"Buoyancy of wood revetments","text":"河岸枯木或根盤可提供粗糙棲地，也可能在洪水中浮起。木材自重與排水體積必須用同一含水狀態比較，部分浸水時不能使用完整體積計算浮力。","textEn":"Wood and rootwads create rough habitat but may lift during floods. Compare weight and displaced volume at a consistent moisture state, and use submerged volume for partial immersion.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：木構的淨浮力除以錨點數就是每支錨具唯一荷載 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Net buoyancy divided by anchor count is the only load on each anchor Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「木構護岸的浮力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Buoyancy of wood revetments\" is correct?","options":["木構的淨浮力除以錨點數就是每支錨具唯一荷載","河岸枯木或根盤可提供粗糙棲地，也可能在洪水中浮起。","剩餘埋深為正就代表護岸在所有洪水下都穩定"],"optionsEn":["Net buoyancy divided by anchor count is the only load on each anchor","Wood and rootwads create rough habitat but may lift during floods.","Any positive remaining embedment proves stability under every flood"],"answer":1,"explanation":"河岸枯木或根盤可提供粗糙棲地，也可能在洪水中浮起。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Wood and rootwads create rough habitat but may lift during floods. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b276-v15-14","title":"木構護岸的浮力：定量估算","titleEn":"Buoyancy of wood revetments: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「木構護岸的浮力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Buoyancy of wood revetments” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhow=1000 kg/m3; rhol=600 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=0.8 m3; Fu=(rhow-rhol)*g*V=3139.2 N。適用邊界：完全浸沒且密度均勻，僅計靜水淨上浮力，不是錨具額定需求。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhow=1000 kg/m3; rhol=600 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=0.8 m3; Fu=(rhow-rhol)*g*V=3139.2 N. Applicable boundary: Fully submerged uniform density; calculates net hydrostatic uplift only, not an anchorage rating. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先量木構尺寸與濕重，再以部分浸水試驗檢查排水量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure geometry and wet mass, then check displacement during partial immersion.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhow=1000 kg/m3; rhol=600 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=0.8 m3; Fu=(rhow-rhol)*g*V=3139.2 N。適用邊界：完全浸沒且密度均勻，僅計靜水淨上浮力，不是錨具額定需求。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhow=1000 kg/m3; rhol=600 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=0.8 m3; Fu=(rhow-rhol)*g*V=3139.2 N. Applicable boundary: Fully submerged uniform density; calculates net hydrostatic uplift only, not an anchorage rating.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「木構護岸的浮力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Buoyancy of wood revetments\", which statement holds?","options":["採購總面積等於完工後不重疊的有效覆蓋面積","下游濃度下降就足以證明護岸永久移除了同等比例泥砂","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhow=1000 kg/m3; rhol=600 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=0.8 m3; Fu=(rhow-rhol)*g*V=3139.2 N。"],"optionsEn":["Purchased material area equals the effective nonoverlapping area after installation","Lower downstream concentration alone proves permanent removal of the same sediment fraction","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhow=1000 kg/m3."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhow=1000 kg/m3; rhol=600 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=0.8 m3; Fu=(rhow-rhol)*g*V=3139.2 N。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhow=1000 kg/m3; rhol=600 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=0.8 m3; Fu=(rhow-rhol)*g*V=3139.2 N. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b276-v15-15","title":"木構護岸的浮力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Buoyancy of wood revetments: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「木構護岸的浮力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Buoyancy of wood revetments” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先量木構尺寸與濕重，再以部分浸水試驗檢查排水量。洪水後記錄轉角、接頭滑移與岸土流失，將浮力計算和現場受力方向比對，若受力不共線則增加力矩分析與接頭試驗。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure geometry and wet mass, then check displacement during partial immersion. After floods, record rotation, connection movement and soil loss. Compare the buoyancy direction with observed loading and add moment analysis when forces are not aligned. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較木材密度增加到八百公斤每立方公尺後的淨浮力，另畫一個岸趾淘空的偏心支承圖，指出還缺哪些尺寸才能計算錨點受力。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate uplift for timber density of eight hundred kilograms per cubic metre. Draw an eccentric support after toe erosion and identify the additional dimensions needed to resolve anchor forces and moments.","failure":"注意干擾：岸土被淘空後木構可能繞剩餘錨點旋轉，接頭受撬力而非單純拉力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Erosion can leave timber rotating about one anchor, prying connections instead of loading them in simple tension. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先量木構尺寸與濕重，再以部分浸水試驗檢查排水量。洪水後記錄轉角、接頭滑移與岸土流失，將浮力計算和現場受力方向比對，若受力不共線則增加力矩分析與接頭試驗。","textEn":"Measure geometry and wet mass, then check displacement during partial immersion. After floods, record rotation, connection movement and soil loss. Compare the buoyancy direction with observed loading and add moment analysis when forces are not aligned.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較木材密度增加到八百公斤每立方公尺後的淨浮力，另畫一個岸趾淘空的偏心支承圖，指出還缺哪些尺寸才能計算錨點受力。","textEn":"Recalculate uplift for timber density of eight hundred kilograms per cubic metre. Draw an eccentric support after toe erosion and identify the additional dimensions needed to resolve anchor forces and moments.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「木構護岸的浮力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Buoyancy of wood revetments\"?","options":["先量木構尺寸與濕重，再以部分浸水試驗檢查排水量。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","河段平均剪力就是每一處岸坡承受的最大剪力"],"optionsEn":["Measure geometry and wet mass, then check displacement during partial immersion.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Reach average shear is the maximum stress at every bank location"],"answer":0,"explanation":"先量木構尺寸與濕重，再以部分浸水試驗檢查排水量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure geometry and wet mass, then check displacement during partial immersion. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b276-v15-16","title":"木構護岸的浮力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Buoyancy of wood revetments: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「木構護岸的浮力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Buoyancy of wood revetments” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"岸土被淘空後木構可能繞剩餘錨點旋轉，接頭受撬力而非單純拉力。只用淨浮力除以錨點數，會掩蓋負荷分配不均及漸進破壞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Erosion can leave timber rotating about one anchor, prying connections instead of loading them in simple tension. Dividing uplift equally among anchors hides unequal distribution and progressive connection failure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：木構隨浸泡吸水與腐朽改變密度，因此檢查不能只依新材出廠重量，還需辨認失去土體包覆後的受力路徑。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Inspection therefore needs the evolving load path after surrounding soil erodes, rather than relying solely on the weight of freshly supplied timber.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「木構的淨浮力除以錨點數就是每支錨具唯一荷載」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Net buoyancy divided by anchor count is the only load on each anchor\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"岸土被淘空後木構可能繞剩餘錨點旋轉，接頭受撬力而非單純拉力。只用淨浮力除以錨點數，會掩蓋負荷分配不均及漸進破壞。","textEn":"Erosion can leave timber rotating about one anchor, prying connections instead of loading them in simple tension. Dividing uplift equally among anchors hides unequal distribution and progressive connection failure.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「木構護岸的浮力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Buoyancy of wood revetments\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","岸土被淘空後木構可能繞剩餘錨點旋轉，接頭受撬力而非單純拉力。","剩餘埋深為正就代表護岸在所有洪水下都穩定"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Erosion can leave timber rotating about one anchor, prying connections instead of loading them in simple tension.","Any positive remaining embedment proves stability under every flood"],"answer":1,"explanation":"岸土被淘空後木構可能繞剩餘錨點旋轉，接頭受撬力而非單純拉力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Erosion can leave timber rotating about one anchor, prying connections instead of loading them in simple tension. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b276-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」與「建立期植株存活率」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Toe embedment and erosion allowance\" and \"Plant survival during establishment\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b276-v15-17","title":"岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Toe embedment and erosion allowance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Toe embedment and erosion allowance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"植生護岸常由岸趾流失開始失去支承，因此埋深應相對於可變河床而非單一施工測點。扣除一次量測沖刷深度能得到幾何餘量，但尚未考慮洪水規模、長期下切與橫向深槽遷移。埋得更深也可能增加施工擾動與地下水交換阻力。合理比較需要把施工基準、自然河床高程與預期變化分開記錄，再以重複測線判斷餘量如何消耗。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Vegetated protection often loses support when its toe erodes. Embedment must therefore reference a changing bed rather than one construction survey point. Subtracting observed scour gives geometric reserve but omits larger floods, long term incision and lateral thalweg migration. Greater embedment can also increase disturbance or obstruct groundwater exchange. Separate construction datum, natural bed elevation and expected change, then use repeated cross sections to track how the reserve is consumed over time. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Toe embedment and erosion allowance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「剩餘埋深為正就代表護岸在所有洪水下都穩定」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any positive remaining embedment proves stability under every flood\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Toe embedment and erosion allowance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-17-k1","title":"岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量","titleEn":"Toe embedment and erosion allowance","text":"植生護岸常由岸趾流失開始失去支承，因此埋深應相對於可變河床而非單一施工測點。扣除一次量測沖刷深度能得到幾何餘量，但尚未考慮洪水規模、長期下切與橫向深槽遷移。","textEn":"Vegetated protection often loses support when its toe erodes. Embedment must therefore reference a changing bed rather than one construction survey point.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：剩餘埋深為正就代表護岸在所有洪水下都穩定 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any positive remaining embedment proves stability under every flood Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Toe embedment and erosion allowance\" is correct?","options":["剩餘埋深為正就代表護岸在所有洪水下都穩定","原始植株存活百分比就是護岸抗剪強度保留百分比","植生護岸常由岸趾流失開始失去支承，因此埋深應相對於可變河床而非單一施工測點。"],"optionsEn":["Any positive remaining embedment proves stability under every flood","The surviving percentage of original plants equals the retained percentage of bank shear strength","Vegetated protection often loses support when its toe erodes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"植生護岸常由岸趾流失開始失去支承，因此埋深應相對於可變河床而非單一施工測點。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Vegetated protection often loses support when its toe erodes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b276-v15-18","title":"岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量：定量估算","titleEn":"Toe embedment and erosion allowance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Toe embedment and erosion allowance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m。適用邊界：同一垂直基準的幾何差值，沒有將剩餘埋深換算成穩定安全係數。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m. Applicable boundary: A geometric difference on one vertical datum, without converting remaining embedment into a stability factor. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在護岸前緣設固定測線並保留基準點，洪水前後用相同方法重測。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Establish fixed transects and preserve survey benchmarks.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m。適用邊界：同一垂直基準的幾何差值，沒有將剩餘埋深換算成穩定安全係數。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m. Applicable boundary: A geometric difference on one vertical datum, without converting remaining embedment into a stability factor.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Toe embedment and erosion allowance\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m。","岸面已經乾燥就代表深處孔隙水壓已完全消散","處理區植被增加的全部百分點都必然由護岸工程造成"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m.","A dry bank surface proves that deeper pore water pressure has completely dissipated","Every percentage point of vegetation gain in the treated reach must be caused by the works"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b276-v15-19","title":"岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Toe embedment and erosion allowance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Toe embedment and erosion allowance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在護岸前緣設固定測線並保留基準點，洪水前後用相同方法重測。將最大沖刷與回淤分列，避免以事後填回的河床掩蓋洪峰侵蝕，並檢查岸趾是否出現空洞或局部懸空。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Establish fixed transects and preserve survey benchmarks. Repeat measurements consistently before and after floods. Separate maximum scour from later deposition, because a refilled bed can conceal peak erosion; inspect for submerged voids or locally unsupported toe sections. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：假設第二次事件再降低河床三十公分，更新幾何餘量並說明為何仍無法宣布安全。規劃兩條新增測線以捕捉深槽側移，標出與舊基準的連結。","observationEn":"Site practice: Lower the bed another thirty centimetres and update the reserve without declaring stability. Place two additional transects to detect lateral thalweg migration and show how they connect to the original survey datum.","failure":"注意干擾：若深槽移到護岸外緣，先前測線可能漏掉局部淘空。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A migrating thalweg may create local undermining between previous transects. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在護岸前緣設固定測線並保留基準點，洪水前後用相同方法重測。將最大沖刷與回淤分列，避免以事後填回的河床掩蓋洪峰侵蝕，並檢查岸趾是否出現空洞或局部懸空。","textEn":"Establish fixed transects and preserve survey benchmarks. Repeat measurements consistently before and after floods. Separate maximum scour from later deposition, because a refilled bed can conceal peak erosion; inspect for submerged voids or locally unsupported toe sections.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"假設第二次事件再降低河床三十公分，更新幾何餘量並說明為何仍無法宣布安全。規劃兩條新增測線以捕捉深槽側移，標出與舊基準的連結。","textEn":"Lower the bed another thirty centimetres and update the reserve without declaring stability. Place two additional transects to detect lateral thalweg migration and show how they connect to the original survey datum.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Toe embedment and erosion allowance\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在護岸前緣設固定測線並保留基準點，洪水前後用相同方法重測。","種植面積可以直接代替所有莖葉的迎流投影面積"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Establish fixed transects and preserve survey benchmarks.","Planted ground area directly equals the frontal area of all stems"],"answer":1,"explanation":"在護岸前緣設固定測線並保留基準點，洪水前後用相同方法重測。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Establish fixed transects and preserve survey benchmarks. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b276-v15-20","title":"岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Toe embedment and erosion allowance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Toe embedment and erosion allowance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若深槽移到護岸外緣，先前測線可能漏掉局部淘空。表面仍貼合的護岸不代表底部有支承，需用水下測量確認邊界是否改變。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A migrating thalweg may create local undermining between previous transects. An apparently flush surface does not prove support underneath; underwater surveys must check whether the erosion boundary has shifted. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：合理比較需要把施工基準、自然河床高程與預期變化分開記錄，再以重複測線判斷餘量如何消耗。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Separate construction datum, natural bed elevation and expected change, then use repeated cross sections to track how the reserve is consumed over time.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「剩餘埋深為正就代表護岸在所有洪水下都穩定」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any positive remaining embedment proves stability under every flood\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若深槽移到護岸外緣，先前測線可能漏掉局部淘空。表面仍貼合的護岸不代表底部有支承，需用水下測量確認邊界是否改變。","textEn":"A migrating thalweg may create local undermining between previous transects. An apparently flush surface does not prove support underneath; underwater surveys must check whether the erosion boundary has shifted.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Toe embedment and erosion allowance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","原始植株存活百分比就是護岸抗剪強度保留百分比","若深槽移到護岸外緣，先前測線可能漏掉局部淘空。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","The surviving percentage of original plants equals the retained percentage of bank shear strength","A migrating thalweg may create local undermining between previous transects."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若深槽移到護岸外緣，先前測線可能漏掉局部淘空。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A migrating thalweg may create local undermining between previous transects. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b276-v15-21","title":"建立期植株存活率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Plant survival during establishment: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「建立期植株存活率」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Plant survival during establishment” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"生態護岸的功能會隨植物建立而演變，栽植後存活率只是其中一個可重複觀察的指標。萌芽、根系延伸與土壤覆蓋不同步，存活的插穗也可能尚未穿過潛在沖蝕面。調查應追蹤固定植株群並記錄洪水、乾旱與補植，避免把後來新增的植株混入原始分母。比較坡位與物種可找出適生限制，但不能由存活百分比直接推算抗剪強度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「建立期植株存活率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Bioengineered protection evolves as plants establish, and survival is one repeatable indicator among several. Budding, root extension and soil cover develop at different rates; a living cutting may not yet cross an erosion plane. Track a fixed cohort and record floods, drought and replacements so newly planted individuals do not contaminate the original denominator. Compare species and bank elevations to investigate suitability, without converting survival percentage directly into shear resistance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Plant survival during establishment” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「原始植株存活百分比就是護岸抗剪強度保留百分比」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The surviving percentage of original plants equals the retained percentage of bank shear strength\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「建立期植株存活率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Plant survival during establishment”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-21-k1","title":"建立期植株存活率","titleEn":"Plant survival during establishment","text":"生態護岸的功能會隨植物建立而演變，栽植後存活率只是其中一個可重複觀察的指標。萌芽、根系延伸與土壤覆蓋不同步，存活的插穗也可能尚未穿過潛在沖蝕面。","textEn":"Bioengineered protection evolves as plants establish, and survival is one repeatable indicator among several. Budding, root extension and soil cover develop at different rates; a living cutting may not yet cross an erosion plane.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：原始植株存活百分比就是護岸抗剪強度保留百分比 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The surviving percentage of original plants equals the retained percentage of bank shear strength Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「建立期植株存活率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Plant survival during establishment\" is correct?","options":["生態護岸的功能會隨植物建立而演變，栽植後存活率只是其中一個可重複觀察的指標。","原始植株存活百分比就是護岸抗剪強度保留百分比","採購總面積等於完工後不重疊的有效覆蓋面積"],"optionsEn":["Bioengineered protection evolves as plants establish, and survival is one repeatable indicator among several.","The surviving percentage of original plants equals the retained percentage of bank shear strength","Purchased material area equals the effective nonoverlapping area after installation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"生態護岸的功能會隨植物建立而演變，栽植後存活率只是其中一個可重複觀察的指標。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Bioengineered protection evolves as plants establish, and survival is one repeatable indicator among several. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b276-v15-22","title":"建立期植株存活率：定量估算","titleEn":"Plant survival during establishment: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「建立期植株存活率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Plant survival during establishment” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless。適用邊界：固定原始植株群的觀察比例，不含補植且不是抗剪能力比例。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Observed proportion of the fixed original cohort, excluding replacements and not representing a shear strength ratio. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：為原始植株編號，在相同季節重訪並明確定義存活，例如有活體芽或組織。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Tag the original cohort and revisit in the same season with an explicit definition of survival.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless。適用邊界：固定原始植株群的觀察比例，不含補植且不是抗剪能力比例。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Observed proportion of the fixed original cohort, excluding replacements and not representing a shear strength ratio.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「建立期植株存活率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Plant survival during establishment\", which statement holds?","options":["下游濃度下降就足以證明護岸永久移除了同等比例泥砂","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless。","河段平均剪力就是每一處岸坡承受的最大剪力"],"optionsEn":["Lower downstream concentration alone proves permanent removal of the same sediment fraction","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless.","Reach average shear is the maximum stress at every bank location"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b276-v15-23","title":"建立期植株存活率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Plant survival during establishment: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「建立期植株存活率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Plant survival during establishment” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"為原始植株編號，在相同季節重訪並明確定義存活，例如有活體芽或組織。另記失蹤、確認死亡及無法判定的數量，補植單獨建帳，再依坡位比較，避免淹水區漏查造成偏差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Tag the original cohort and revisit in the same season with an explicit definition of survival. Record missing, confirmed dead and uncertain plants separately. Keep replacements in another register and compare bank elevations to detect incomplete field survey bias. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將失蹤但未確認死亡的二十株分別視為存活及死亡，建立上下界。再設計一個不破壞整片護岸的根區抽樣方案，說明抽樣如何連結功能判讀。","observationEn":"Site practice: Treat twenty missing plants alternately as alive and dead to construct bounds. Design a limited root-zone sampling programme and explain how those observations would connect survival records with the intended protective function.","failure":"注意干擾：補植後若把新株計入存活數而沿用原始分母，會高估建立成功。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Counting replacement plants against the original denominator exaggerates establishment success. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"為原始植株編號，在相同季節重訪並明確定義存活，例如有活體芽或組織。另記失蹤、確認死亡及無法判定的數量，補植單獨建帳，再依坡位比較，避免淹水區漏查造成偏差。","textEn":"Tag the original cohort and revisit in the same season with an explicit definition of survival. Record missing, confirmed dead and uncertain plants separately. Keep replacements in another register and compare bank elevations to detect incomplete field survey bias.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將失蹤但未確認死亡的二十株分別視為存活及死亡，建立上下界。再設計一個不破壞整片護岸的根區抽樣方案，說明抽樣如何連結功能判讀。","textEn":"Treat twenty missing plants alternately as alive and dead to construct bounds. Design a limited root-zone sampling programme and explain how those observations would connect survival records with the intended protective function.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「建立期植株存活率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Plant survival during establishment\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","表層根系密度可直接代表任何深度滑動面的補強能力","為原始植株編號，在相同季節重訪並明確定義存活，例如有活體芽或組織。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Surface root density directly represents reinforcement on a failure plane at any depth","Tag the original cohort and revisit in the same season with an explicit definition of survival."],"answer":2,"explanation":"為原始植株編號，在相同季節重訪並明確定義存活，例如有活體芽或組織。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Tag the original cohort and revisit in the same season with an explicit definition of survival. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b276-v15-24","title":"建立期植株存活率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Plant survival during establishment: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「建立期植株存活率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Plant survival during establishment” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"補植後若把新株計入存活數而沿用原始分母，會高估建立成功。另一方面，短期綠葉也可能掩蓋根部腐爛，需結合根區與土壤觀察。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Counting replacement plants against the original denominator exaggerates establishment success. Short lived foliage can also conceal root decay, so survival counts need observations of root conditions and surrounding soil. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較坡位與物種可找出適生限制，但不能由存活百分比直接推算抗剪強度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare species and bank elevations to investigate suitability, without converting survival percentage directly into shear resistance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「原始植株存活百分比就是護岸抗剪強度保留百分比」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The surviving percentage of original plants equals the retained percentage of bank shear strength\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"補植後若把新株計入存活數而沿用原始分母，會高估建立成功。另一方面，短期綠葉也可能掩蓋根部腐爛，需結合根區與土壤觀察。","textEn":"Counting replacement plants against the original denominator exaggerates establishment success. Short lived foliage can also conceal root decay, so survival counts need observations of root conditions and surrounding soil.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「建立期植株存活率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Plant survival during establishment\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補植後若把新株計入存活數而沿用原始分母，會高估建立成功。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","採購總面積等於完工後不重疊的有效覆蓋面積"],"optionsEn":["Counting replacement plants against the original denominator exaggerates establishment success.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Purchased material area equals the effective nonoverlapping area after installation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"補植後若把新株計入存活數而沿用原始分母，會高估建立成功。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Counting replacement plants against the original denominator exaggerates establishment success. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b276-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」與「退水期孔隙水壓」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Mat overlap and effective coverage\" and \"Pore pressure during drawdown\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b276-v15-25","title":"纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Mat overlap and effective coverage: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Mat overlap and effective coverage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"椰纖維毯的採購面積不等於實際覆蓋面積，搭接、端部固定與曲面貼合都會消耗材料。搭接方向要配合水流，避免迎流邊緣掀起後使水在毯下集中。相鄰條帶需保持連續接觸土面，懸空會讓幼根難以穿入，也會形成沖蝕通道。數量估算可以先用平面幾何，但施工驗收還要檢查坡面展長、固定點與排水，不能用足量材料替代安裝品質。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Purchased coir mat area differs from effective cover because seams, end anchorage and surface conformity consume material. Orient overlaps with flow so exposed edges do not lift and channel water underneath. Adjacent strips need continuous soil contact; bridging can obstruct root establishment and create erosion pathways. Begin quantities with planar geometry, then inspect slope length, fixings and drainage. Delivering enough material does not demonstrate that the installation transfers loads or supports vegetation as intended. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Mat overlap and effective coverage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2.","failure":"常見誤解：「採購總面積等於完工後不重疊的有效覆蓋面積」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Purchased material area equals the effective nonoverlapping area after installation\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Mat overlap and effective coverage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-25-k1","title":"纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋","titleEn":"Mat overlap and effective coverage","text":"椰纖維毯的採購面積不等於實際覆蓋面積，搭接、端部固定與曲面貼合都會消耗材料。搭接方向要配合水流，避免迎流邊緣掀起後使水在毯下集中。","textEn":"Purchased coir mat area differs from effective cover because seams, end anchorage and surface conformity consume material. Orient overlaps with flow so exposed edges do not lift and channel water underneath.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：採購總面積等於完工後不重疊的有效覆蓋面積 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Purchased material area equals the effective nonoverlapping area after installation Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Mat overlap and effective coverage\" is correct?","options":["採購總面積等於完工後不重疊的有效覆蓋面積","椰纖維毯的採購面積不等於實際覆蓋面積，搭接、端部固定與曲面貼合都會消耗材料。","岸面已經乾燥就代表深處孔隙水壓已完全消散"],"optionsEn":["Purchased material area equals the effective nonoverlapping area after installation","Purchased coir mat area differs from effective cover because seams, end anchorage and surface conformity consume material.","A dry bank surface proves that deeper pore water pressure has completely dissipated"],"answer":1,"explanation":"椰纖維毯的採購面積不等於實際覆蓋面積，搭接、端部固定與曲面貼合都會消耗材料。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Purchased coir mat area differs from effective cover because seams, end anchorage and surface conformity consume material. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b276-v15-26","title":"纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋：定量估算","titleEn":"Mat overlap and effective coverage: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Mat overlap and effective coverage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2。適用邊界：平面平行條帶僅計五道縱向搭接，未扣端部與曲面裁切。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2. Applicable boundary: Parallel planar strips with five longitudinal overlaps only; excludes end anchorage and curved trimming. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在展開圖上逐條標出淨寬與搭接，不把每條兩側都重複扣除。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark net width and seams strip by strip without subtracting every edge twice.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2。適用邊界：平面平行條帶僅計五道縱向搭接，未扣端部與曲面裁切。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2. Applicable boundary: Parallel planar strips with five longitudinal overlaps only; excludes end anchorage and curved trimming.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Mat overlap and effective coverage\", which statement holds?","options":["處理區植被增加的全部百分點都必然由護岸工程造成","種植面積可以直接代替所有莖葉的迎流投影面積","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2。"],"optionsEn":["Every percentage point of vegetation gain in the treated reach must be caused by the works","Planted ground area directly equals the frontal area of all stems","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b276-v15-27","title":"纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Mat overlap and effective coverage: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Mat overlap and effective coverage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在展開圖上逐條標出淨寬與搭接，不把每條兩側都重複扣除。現場用卷尺抽驗搭接和坡面貼合，灑少量清水觀察是否沿毯下集中，再另列端部埋設與修剪損耗。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark net width and seams strip by strip without subtracting every edge twice. Check overlap and soil contact in the field. A small controlled water application can reveal underflow; record end anchorage and trimming losses separately. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把搭接改為三十公分重新計算淨覆蓋，並畫出彎曲岸坡需要裁切的位置。將幾何損耗與安裝缺失分成兩項，提出各自的驗收證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase overlap to thirty centimetres and recalculate effective coverage. Draw where a curved bank requires trimming, distinguish geometric waste from installation defects, and specify separate acceptance evidence for those two issues.","failure":"注意干擾：材料總面積足夠但接縫逆流或鬆弛時，水會掀毯並從下方沖走細土。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Adequate total material can still fail when loose or upstream-facing seams lift. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在展開圖上逐條標出淨寬與搭接，不把每條兩側都重複扣除。現場用卷尺抽驗搭接和坡面貼合，灑少量清水觀察是否沿毯下集中，再另列端部埋設與修剪損耗。","textEn":"Mark net width and seams strip by strip without subtracting every edge twice. Check overlap and soil contact in the field. A small controlled water application can reveal underflow; record end anchorage and trimming losses separately.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把搭接改為三十公分重新計算淨覆蓋，並畫出彎曲岸坡需要裁切的位置。將幾何損耗與安裝缺失分成兩項，提出各自的驗收證據。","textEn":"Increase overlap to thirty centimetres and recalculate effective coverage. Draw where a curved bank requires trimming, distinguish geometric waste from installation defects, and specify separate acceptance evidence for those two issues.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Mat overlap and effective coverage\"?","options":["在展開圖上逐條標出淨寬與搭接，不把每條兩側都重複扣除。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","木構的淨浮力除以錨點數就是每支錨具唯一荷載"],"optionsEn":["Mark net width and seams strip by strip without subtracting every edge twice.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Net buoyancy divided by anchor count is the only load on each anchor"],"answer":0,"explanation":"在展開圖上逐條標出淨寬與搭接，不把每條兩側都重複扣除。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark net width and seams strip by strip without subtracting every edge twice. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b276-v15-28","title":"纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋：失效診斷","titleEn":"Mat overlap and effective coverage: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Mat overlap and effective coverage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"材料總面積足夠但接縫逆流或鬆弛時，水會掀毯並從下方沖走細土。裸露小縫可能擴大成集中溝，應追查接縫方向及固定點。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Adequate total material can still fail when loose or upstream-facing seams lift. Water then removes soil beneath the mat, turning small openings into channels; inspect seam orientation and fixing locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：數量估算可以先用平面幾何，但施工驗收還要檢查坡面展長、固定點與排水，不能用足量材料替代安裝品質。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Delivering enough material does not demonstrate that the installation transfers loads or supports vegetation as intended.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「採購總面積等於完工後不重疊的有效覆蓋面積」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Purchased material area equals the effective nonoverlapping area after installation\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"材料總面積足夠但接縫逆流或鬆弛時，水會掀毯並從下方沖走細土。裸露小縫可能擴大成集中溝，應追查接縫方向及固定點。","textEn":"Adequate total material can still fail when loose or upstream-facing seams lift. Water then removes soil beneath the mat, turning small openings into channels; inspect seam orientation and fixing locations.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Mat overlap and effective coverage\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","材料總面積足夠但接縫逆流或鬆弛時，水會掀毯並從下方沖走細土。","岸面已經乾燥就代表深處孔隙水壓已完全消散"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Adequate total material can still fail when loose or upstream-facing seams lift.","A dry bank surface proves that deeper pore water pressure has completely dissipated"],"answer":1,"explanation":"材料總面積足夠但接縫逆流或鬆弛時，水會掀毯並從下方沖走細土。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Adequate total material can still fail when loose or upstream-facing seams lift. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b276-v15-29","title":"退水期孔隙水壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pore pressure during drawdown: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「退水期孔隙水壓」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pore pressure during drawdown” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"洪水退去後，河道側支承水壓可能先降低，而岸土內水位仍高，產生朝河道的滲流與較低有效應力。植物蒸散不能在短時間內保證消除這種壓差，根系補強也不取代排水條件分析。以水頭差估算孔壓只能描述指定位置與假定連通狀態，真實退水過程還受滲透係數、層理與儲水性控制。監測應把河水位與岸內孔壓時間序列同步對齊。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「退水期孔隙水壓」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After a flood, river support pressure may fall before pore pressures inside the bank dissipate, promoting outward seepage and reducing effective stress. Plant transpiration cannot guarantee rapid relief, and roots do not replace drainage analysis. A head difference estimates pressure at a specified point under assumed connectivity, while actual drawdown depends on permeability, layering and storage. Synchronize river stage and internal piezometer records to distinguish transient pressure lag from static groundwater conditions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pore pressure during drawdown” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「岸面已經乾燥就代表深處孔隙水壓已完全消散」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A dry bank surface proves that deeper pore water pressure has completely dissipated\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「退水期孔隙水壓」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pore pressure during drawdown”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-29-k1","title":"退水期孔隙水壓","titleEn":"Pore pressure during drawdown","text":"洪水退去後，河道側支承水壓可能先降低，而岸土內水位仍高，產生朝河道的滲流與較低有效應力。植物蒸散不能在短時間內保證消除這種壓差，根系補強也不取代排水條件分析。","textEn":"After a flood, river support pressure may fall before pore pressures inside the bank dissipate, promoting outward seepage and reducing effective stress. Plant transpiration cannot guarantee rapid relief, and roots do not replace drainage analysis.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岸面已經乾燥就代表深處孔隙水壓已完全消散 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A dry bank surface proves that deeper pore water pressure has completely dissipated Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「退水期孔隙水壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pore pressure during drawdown\" is correct?","options":["岸面已經乾燥就代表深處孔隙水壓已完全消散","下游濃度下降就足以證明護岸永久移除了同等比例泥砂","洪水退去後，河道側支承水壓可能先降低，而岸土內水位仍高，產生朝河道的滲流與較低有效應力。"],"optionsEn":["A dry bank surface proves that deeper pore water pressure has completely dissipated","Lower downstream concentration alone proves permanent removal of the same sediment fraction","After a flood, river support pressure may fall before pore pressures inside the bank dissipate, promoting outward seepage and reducing effective stress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"洪水退去後，河道側支承水壓可能先降低，而岸土內水位仍高，產生朝河道的滲流與較低有效應力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After a flood, river support pressure may fall before pore pressures inside the bank dissipate, promoting outward seepage and reducing effective stress. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b276-v15-30","title":"退水期孔隙水壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Pore pressure during drawdown: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「退水期孔隙水壓」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pore pressure during drawdown” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa。適用邊界：同一高程兩點之靜水壓差示例，不求解非定常滲流或整體穩定。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa. Applicable boundary: Illustrates hydrostatic pressure difference at one elevation, without solving transient seepage or overall stability. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在岸內不同深度設孔壓量測點，與河水位使用同一高程及時鐘。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Place piezometers at different depths and use a common datum and clock with river stage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa。適用邊界：同一高程兩點之靜水壓差示例，不求解非定常滲流或整體穩定。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa. Applicable boundary: Illustrates hydrostatic pressure difference at one elevation, without solving transient seepage or overall stability.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「退水期孔隙水壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pore pressure during drawdown\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa。","河段平均剪力就是每一處岸坡承受的最大剪力","表層根系密度可直接代表任何深度滑動面的補強能力"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa.","Reach average shear is the maximum stress at every bank location","Surface root density directly represents reinforcement on a failure plane at any depth"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b276-v15-31","title":"退水期孔隙水壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pore pressure during drawdown: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「退水期孔隙水壓」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pore pressure during drawdown” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在岸內不同深度設孔壓量測點，與河水位使用同一高程及時鐘。退水時比較峰值與延遲，並查看排水出口是否阻塞；若土層反應差異大，應分層建模而非平均所有孔壓。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Place piezometers at different depths and use a common datum and clock with river stage. Compare pressure peaks and delays during drawdown, inspect drainage outlets, and model distinct layers separately when their measured pressure responses differ substantially. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：假設河水再降五十公分而岸內水頭未變，重算壓差。畫出兩條可能的消散曲線，指出需要多長的觀測紀錄才能分辨快速與緩慢排水。","observationEn":"Site practice: Lower river stage another fifty centimetres while holding internal head fixed and recalculate the pressure difference. Sketch fast and slow dissipation curves and specify monitoring duration needed to distinguish the two responses.","failure":"注意干擾：不透水夾層可能保留高孔壓，岸面看似乾燥卻仍有深層滑動風險。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A low permeability layer may retain pressure beneath a dry-looking surface. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在岸內不同深度設孔壓量測點，與河水位使用同一高程及時鐘。退水時比較峰值與延遲，並查看排水出口是否阻塞；若土層反應差異大，應分層建模而非平均所有孔壓。","textEn":"Place piezometers at different depths and use a common datum and clock with river stage. Compare pressure peaks and delays during drawdown, inspect drainage outlets, and model distinct layers separately when their measured pressure responses differ substantially.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"假設河水再降五十公分而岸內水頭未變，重算壓差。畫出兩條可能的消散曲線，指出需要多長的觀測紀錄才能分辨快速與緩慢排水。","textEn":"Lower river stage another fifty centimetres while holding internal head fixed and recalculate the pressure difference. Sketch fast and slow dissipation curves and specify monitoring duration needed to distinguish the two responses.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「退水期孔隙水壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pore pressure during drawdown\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在岸內不同深度設孔壓量測點，與河水位使用同一高程及時鐘。","剩餘埋深為正就代表護岸在所有洪水下都穩定"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Place piezometers at different depths and use a common datum and clock with river stage.","Any positive remaining embedment proves stability under every flood"],"answer":1,"explanation":"在岸內不同深度設孔壓量測點，與河水位使用同一高程及時鐘。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Place piezometers at different depths and use a common datum and clock with river stage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b276-v15-32","title":"退水期孔隙水壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pore pressure during drawdown: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「退水期孔隙水壓」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pore pressure during drawdown” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不透水夾層可能保留高孔壓，岸面看似乾燥卻仍有深層滑動風險。若只量地表含水率，會誤判退水後已恢復承載能力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A low permeability layer may retain pressure beneath a dry-looking surface. Surface moisture alone can therefore suggest recovered resistance while deeper parts of the bank remain vulnerable to sliding. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：監測應把河水位與岸內孔壓時間序列同步對齊。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Synchronize river stage and internal piezometer records to distinguish transient pressure lag from static groundwater conditions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岸面已經乾燥就代表深處孔隙水壓已完全消散」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A dry bank surface proves that deeper pore water pressure has completely dissipated\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不透水夾層可能保留高孔壓，岸面看似乾燥卻仍有深層滑動風險。若只量地表含水率，會誤判退水後已恢復承載能力。","textEn":"A low permeability layer may retain pressure beneath a dry-looking surface. Surface moisture alone can therefore suggest recovered resistance while deeper parts of the bank remain vulnerable to sliding.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「退水期孔隙水壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pore pressure during drawdown\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","下游濃度下降就足以證明護岸永久移除了同等比例泥砂","不透水夾層可能保留高孔壓，岸面看似乾燥卻仍有深層滑動風險。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Lower downstream concentration alone proves permanent removal of the same sediment fraction","A low permeability layer may retain pressure beneath a dry-looking surface."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不透水夾層可能保留高孔壓，岸面看似乾燥卻仍有深層滑動風險。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A low permeability layer may retain pressure beneath a dry-looking surface. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b276-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」與「對照監測的生態成效」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Sediment flux around bank treatments\" and \"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b276-v15-33","title":"泥砂通量的護岸檢核：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Sediment flux around bank treatments: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sediment flux around bank treatments” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"生態護岸可能攔截細砂，也可能在施工或洪水初期釋出土粒，因此應比較質量通量而非只比較濁度讀數。流量與濃度必須在相同控制體邊界及時段取得，清水側向流入會稀釋濃度卻不代表沉積。輸入減輸出得到的是控制體內暫存與未量側向交換的合計，需要另查床面變化才能歸因。濁度轉濃度關係還會隨粒徑與有機質改變，必須用水樣校準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A treatment may trap fines or release soil during construction and early floods. Compare mass flux rather than turbidity alone, matching discharge and concentration at the same boundaries and times. Clear lateral inflow can dilute concentration without depositing sediment. Inflow minus outflow represents storage plus unmeasured exchanges, requiring bed observations before attribution. The turbidity to concentration relation also changes with grain size and organic material, so physical samples are needed for calibration. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sediment flux around bank treatments” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qin=0.08 m3/s; Cin=0.12 kg/m3; Qout=0.075 m3/s; Cout=0.07 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; dM=(Qin*Cin-Qout*Cout)*dt=15.66 kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qin=0.08 m3/s; Cin=0.12 kg/m3; Qout=0.075 m3/s; Cout=0.07 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; dM=(Qin*Cin-Qout*Cout)*dt=15.66 kg.","failure":"常見誤解：「下游濃度下降就足以證明護岸永久移除了同等比例泥砂」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Lower downstream concentration alone proves permanent removal of the same sediment fraction\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sediment flux around bank treatments”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-33-k1","title":"泥砂通量的護岸檢核","titleEn":"Sediment flux around bank treatments","text":"生態護岸可能攔截細砂，也可能在施工或洪水初期釋出土粒，因此應比較質量通量而非只比較濁度讀數。流量與濃度必須在相同控制體邊界及時段取得，清水側向流入會稀釋濃度卻不代表沉積。","textEn":"A treatment may trap fines or release soil during construction and early floods. Compare mass flux rather than turbidity alone, matching discharge and concentration at the same boundaries and times.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：下游濃度下降就足以證明護岸永久移除了同等比例泥砂 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Lower downstream concentration alone proves permanent removal of the same sediment fraction Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sediment flux around bank treatments\" is correct?","options":["生態護岸可能攔截細砂，也可能在施工或洪水初期釋出土粒，因此應比較質量通量而非只比較濁度讀數。","下游濃度下降就足以證明護岸永久移除了同等比例泥砂","處理區植被增加的全部百分點都必然由護岸工程造成"],"optionsEn":["A treatment may trap fines or release soil during construction and early floods.","Lower downstream concentration alone proves permanent removal of the same sediment fraction","Every percentage point of vegetation gain in the treated reach must be caused by the works"],"answer":0,"explanation":"生態護岸可能攔截細砂，也可能在施工或洪水初期釋出土粒，因此應比較質量通量而非只比較濁度讀數。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A treatment may trap fines or release soil during construction and early floods. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b276-v15-34","title":"泥砂通量的護岸檢核：定量估算","titleEn":"Sediment flux around bank treatments: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sediment flux around bank treatments” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qin=0.08 m3/s; Cin=0.12 kg/m3; Qout=0.075 m3/s; Cout=0.07 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; dM=(Qin*Cin-Qout*Cout)*dt=15.66 kg。適用邊界：一小時定常且無側向泥砂通量，所得為控制體暫存，不能直接宣稱永久去除。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qin=0.08 m3/s; Cin=0.12 kg/m3; Qout=0.075 m3/s; Cout=0.07 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; dM=(Qin*Cin-Qout*Cout)*dt=15.66 kg. Applicable boundary: Steady one-hour interval without lateral sediment flux; result is control-volume storage, not demonstrated permanent removal. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步採集上下游流量與水樣，以實驗室懸浮固體建立濁度校正，再確認是否有排水溝或岸崩加入泥砂。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Collect synchronized upstream and downstream discharge and samples, calibrate turbidity against suspended solids, and identify drains or bank failures adding sediment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qin=0.08 m3/s; Cin=0.12 kg/m3; Qout=0.075 m3/s; Cout=0.07 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; dM=(Qin*Cin-Qout*Cout)*dt=15.66 kg。適用邊界：一小時定常且無側向泥砂通量，所得為控制體暫存，不能直接宣稱永久去除。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qin=0.08 m3/s; Cin=0.12 kg/m3; Qout=0.075 m3/s; Cout=0.07 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; dM=(Qin*Cin-Qout*Cout)*dt=15.66 kg. Applicable boundary: Steady one-hour interval without lateral sediment flux; result is control-volume storage, not demonstrated permanent removal.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sediment flux around bank treatments\", which statement holds?","options":["種植面積可以直接代替所有莖葉的迎流投影面積","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qin=0.08 m3/s; Cin=0.12 kg/m3; Qout=0.075 m3/s; Cout=0.07 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; dM=(Qin*Cin-Qout*Cout)*dt=15.66 kg。","木構的淨浮力除以錨點數就是每支錨具唯一荷載"],"optionsEn":["Planted ground area directly equals the frontal area of all stems","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qin=0.08 m3/s.","Net buoyancy divided by anchor count is the only load on each anchor"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qin=0.08 m3/s; Cin=0.12 kg/m3; Qout=0.075 m3/s; Cout=0.07 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; dM=(Qin*Cin-Qout*Cout)*dt=15.66 kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qin=0.08 m3/s; Cin=0.12 kg/m3; Qout=0.075 m3/s; Cout=0.07 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; dM=(Qin*Cin-Qout*Cout)*dt=15.66 kg. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b276-v15-35","title":"泥砂通量的護岸檢核：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Sediment flux around bank treatments: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sediment flux around bank treatments” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步採集上下游流量與水樣，以實驗室懸浮固體建立濁度校正，再確認是否有排水溝或岸崩加入泥砂。用床面標記或沉積盤驗證暫存方向，並在下一次洪水後查是否重新被帶走。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Collect synchronized upstream and downstream discharge and samples, calibrate turbidity against suspended solids, and identify drains or bank failures adding sediment. Check storage direction with bed markers or traps, then inspect whether the next monitored flood event remobilizes that stored material. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：新增一股已知流量與濃度的側向排水後重寫質量平衡，列出新增量測。比較暫存與永久去除需要的追蹤時間，說明下一場洪水可能如何改變結論。","observationEn":"Site practice: Add a lateral drain with specified flow and concentration, rewrite the mass balance and list new measurements. Compare the monitoring needed for temporary storage and permanent removal, including how another flood could reverse the interpretation.","failure":"注意干擾：若下游被清水稀釋，濃度下降可能被誤報成攔砂成功。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Dilution can make lower concentration appear to prove trapping. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步採集上下游流量與水樣，以實驗室懸浮固體建立濁度校正，再確認是否有排水溝或岸崩加入泥砂。用床面標記或沉積盤驗證暫存方向，並在下一次洪水後查是否重新被帶走。","textEn":"Collect synchronized upstream and downstream discharge and samples, calibrate turbidity against suspended solids, and identify drains or bank failures adding sediment. Check storage direction with bed markers or traps, then inspect whether the next monitored flood event remobilizes that stored material.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"新增一股已知流量與濃度的側向排水後重寫質量平衡，列出新增量測。比較暫存與永久去除需要的追蹤時間，說明下一場洪水可能如何改變結論。","textEn":"Add a lateral drain with specified flow and concentration, rewrite the mass balance and list new measurements. Compare the monitoring needed for temporary storage and permanent removal, including how another flood could reverse the interpretation.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sediment flux around bank treatments\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","原始植株存活百分比就是護岸抗剪強度保留百分比","同步採集上下游流量與水樣，以實驗室懸浮固體建立濁度校正，再確認是否有排水溝或岸崩加入泥砂。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The surviving percentage of original plants equals the retained percentage of bank shear strength","Collect synchronized upstream and downstream discharge and samples, calibrate turbidity against suspended solids, and identify drains or bank failures adding sediment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步採集上下游流量與水樣，以實驗室懸浮固體建立濁度校正，再確認是否有排水溝或岸崩加入泥砂。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Collect synchronized upstream and downstream discharge and samples, calibrate turbidity against suspended solids, and identify drains or bank failures adding sediment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b276-v15-36","title":"泥砂通量的護岸檢核：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sediment flux around bank treatments: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sediment flux around bank treatments” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若下游被清水稀釋，濃度下降可能被誤報成攔砂成功。漏算側向流量或採樣時間錯開，也會製造假質量差，應先閉合水量帳。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Dilution can make lower concentration appear to prove trapping. Missing lateral flows or mismatched sampling times also create false mass differences, so close the water balance before interpreting sediment retention. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：濁度轉濃度關係還會隨粒徑與有機質改變，必須用水樣校準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The turbidity to concentration relation also changes with grain size and organic material, so physical samples are needed for calibration.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「下游濃度下降就足以證明護岸永久移除了同等比例泥砂」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Lower downstream concentration alone proves permanent removal of the same sediment fraction\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若下游被清水稀釋，濃度下降可能被誤報成攔砂成功。漏算側向流量或採樣時間錯開，也會製造假質量差，應先閉合水量帳。","textEn":"Dilution can make lower concentration appear to prove trapping. Missing lateral flows or mismatched sampling times also create false mass differences, so close the water balance before interpreting sediment retention.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sediment flux around bank treatments\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若下游被清水稀釋，濃度下降可能被誤報成攔砂成功。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","處理區植被增加的全部百分點都必然由護岸工程造成"],"optionsEn":["Dilution can make lower concentration appear to prove trapping.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Every percentage point of vegetation gain in the treated reach must be caused by the works"],"answer":0,"explanation":"若下游被清水稀釋，濃度下降可能被誤報成攔砂成功。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Dilution can make lower concentration appear to prove trapping. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b276-v15-37","title":"對照監測的生態成效：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「對照監測的生態成效」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"工程後植被增加可能來自較濕的年份、放牧減少或上游治理，而不完全由護岸措施造成。前後加對照的設計，用未處理區的同期間變化扣除共同背景，能提供比單純前後比較更清楚的證據。對照區仍須有相近坡位、土壤與管理，並避免受工程水流改變影響。覆蓋率是面積比例，差中之差應以百分點表示；它不能單獨代表物種多樣性、棲地品質或結構安全。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「對照監測的生態成效」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Vegetation can increase because a year is wetter, grazing declines or upstream management changes. A before-after comparison with an untreated reach subtracts shared background change and offers stronger evidence than a simple before-after count. The comparison reach still needs similar soils, elevation and management, without receiving the treatment's hydraulic effects. Cover is an area proportion, so the difference in differences uses percentage points and does not independently measure biodiversity, habitat quality or structural safety. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：T0=35 percent; T1=70 percent; C0=40 percent; C1=55 percent; effect=(T1-T0)-(C1-C0)=20 percentage-points。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: T0=35 percent; T1=70 percent; C0=40 percent; C1=55 percent; effect=(T1-T0)-(C1-C0)=20 percentage-points.","failure":"常見誤解：「處理區植被增加的全部百分點都必然由護岸工程造成」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every percentage point of vegetation gain in the treated reach must be caused by the works\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「對照監測的生態成效」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-37-k1","title":"對照監測的生態成效","titleEn":"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring","text":"工程後植被增加可能來自較濕的年份、放牧減少或上游治理，而不完全由護岸措施造成。前後加對照的設計，用未處理區的同期間變化扣除共同背景，能提供比單純前後比較更清楚的證據。","textEn":"Vegetation can increase because a year is wetter, grazing declines or upstream management changes. A before-after comparison with an untreated reach subtracts shared background change and offers stronger evidence than a simple before-after count.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：處理區植被增加的全部百分點都必然由護岸工程造成 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every percentage point of vegetation gain in the treated reach must be caused by the works Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「對照監測的生態成效」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring\" is correct?","options":["處理區植被增加的全部百分點都必然由護岸工程造成","工程後植被增加可能來自較濕的年份、放牧減少或上游治理，而不完全由護岸措施造成。","河段平均剪力就是每一處岸坡承受的最大剪力"],"optionsEn":["Every percentage point of vegetation gain in the treated reach must be caused by the works","Vegetation can increase because a year is wetter, grazing declines or upstream management changes.","Reach average shear is the maximum stress at every bank location"],"answer":1,"explanation":"工程後植被增加可能來自較濕的年份、放牧減少或上游治理，而不完全由護岸措施造成。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Vegetation can increase because a year is wetter, grazing declines or upstream management changes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b276-v15-38","title":"對照監測的生態成效：定量估算","titleEn":"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「對照監測的生態成效」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：T0=35 percent; T1=70 percent; C0=40 percent; C1=55 percent; effect=(T1-T0)-(C1-C0)=20 percentage-points。適用邊界：示範差中之差，因果解釋仍需平行趨勢與不受干擾的對照。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: T0=35 percent; T1=70 percent; C0=40 percent; C1=55 percent; effect=(T1-T0)-(C1-C0)=20 percentage-points. Applicable boundary: Illustrates difference in differences; causal interpretation still requires parallel trends and an unaffected comparison. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在工程前至少重複調查不同季節，確認兩區變化方向是否相近，之後用相同樣方與判讀規則追蹤。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Repeat surveys across seasons before treatment to compare trajectories, then retain the same quadrats and interpretation rules.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：T0=35 percent; T1=70 percent; C0=40 percent; C1=55 percent; effect=(T1-T0)-(C1-C0)=20 percentage-points。適用邊界：示範差中之差，因果解釋仍需平行趨勢與不受干擾的對照。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: T0=35 percent; T1=70 percent; C0=40 percent; C1=55 percent; effect=(T1-T0)-(C1-C0)=20 percentage-points. Applicable boundary: Illustrates difference in differences; causal interpretation still requires parallel trends and an unaffected comparison.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「對照監測的生態成效」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring\", which statement holds?","options":["表層根系密度可直接代表任何深度滑動面的補強能力","剩餘埋深為正就代表護岸在所有洪水下都穩定","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：T0=35 percent; T1=70 percent; C0=40 percent; C1=55 percent; effect=(T1-T0)-(C1-C0)=20 percentage-points。"],"optionsEn":["Surface root density directly represents reinforcement on a failure plane at any depth","Any positive remaining embedment proves stability under every flood","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: T0=35 percent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：T0=35 percent; T1=70 percent; C0=40 percent; C1=55 percent; effect=(T1-T0)-(C1-C0)=20 percentage-points。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: T0=35 percent; T1=70 percent; C0=40 percent; C1=55 percent; effect=(T1-T0)-(C1-C0)=20 percentage-points. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b276-v15-39","title":"對照監測的生態成效：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「對照監測的生態成效」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在工程前至少重複調查不同季節，確認兩區變化方向是否相近，之後用相同樣方與判讀規則追蹤。另記洪水、放牧與補植，若對照區也受到改流影響，應重新界定對照或限制因果結論。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Repeat surveys across seasons before treatment to compare trajectories, then retain the same quadrats and interpretation rules. Record floods, grazing and replanting. If altered flow affects the comparison reach, redefine it or limit the causal claim. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將對照區的後期覆蓋率改成百分之六十五，重算效果並解釋差異。設計一項獨立棲地指標，使覆蓋率改善不會被誤用為所有生態功能均改善的結論。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change later comparison cover to sixty five percent, recompute the effect and explain the difference. Add an independent habitat indicator so increased cover cannot be mistaken for improvement in every ecological function.","failure":"注意干擾：不同年份用不同樣方位置會把空間差異當成工程效果。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Moving quadrats between years confuses spatial differences with treatment effects. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在工程前至少重複調查不同季節，確認兩區變化方向是否相近，之後用相同樣方與判讀規則追蹤。另記洪水、放牧與補植，若對照區也受到改流影響，應重新界定對照或限制因果結論。","textEn":"Repeat surveys across seasons before treatment to compare trajectories, then retain the same quadrats and interpretation rules. Record floods, grazing and replanting. If altered flow affects the comparison reach, redefine it or limit the causal claim.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將對照區的後期覆蓋率改成百分之六十五，重算效果並解釋差異。設計一項獨立棲地指標，使覆蓋率改善不會被誤用為所有生態功能均改善的結論。","textEn":"Change later comparison cover to sixty five percent, recompute the effect and explain the difference. Add an independent habitat indicator so increased cover cannot be mistaken for improvement in every ecological function.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「對照監測的生態成效」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring\"?","options":["在工程前至少重複調查不同季節，確認兩區變化方向是否相近，之後用相同樣方與判讀規則追蹤。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","採購總面積等於完工後不重疊的有效覆蓋面積"],"optionsEn":["Repeat surveys across seasons before treatment to compare trajectories, then retain the same quadrats and interpretation rules.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Purchased material area equals the effective nonoverlapping area after installation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"在工程前至少重複調查不同季節，確認兩區變化方向是否相近，之後用相同樣方與判讀規則追蹤。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Repeat surveys across seasons before treatment to compare trajectories, then retain the same quadrats and interpretation rules. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b276-v15-40","title":"對照監測的生態成效：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「對照監測的生態成效」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不同年份用不同樣方位置會把空間差異當成工程效果。若只選長得好的護岸段，平均覆蓋也會偏高，需事先固定抽樣設計。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Moving quadrats between years confuses spatial differences with treatment effects. Selecting only thriving sections further inflates average cover; fix the sampling design before observing which areas appear successful in the field. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：覆蓋率是面積比例，差中之差應以百分點表示；它不能單獨代表物種多樣性、棲地品質或結構安全。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Cover is an area proportion, so the difference in differences uses percentage points and does not independently measure biodiversity, habitat quality or structural safety.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「處理區植被增加的全部百分點都必然由護岸工程造成」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every percentage point of vegetation gain in the treated reach must be caused by the works\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不同年份用不同樣方位置會把空間差異當成工程效果。若只選長得好的護岸段，平均覆蓋也會偏高，需事先固定抽樣設計。","textEn":"Moving quadrats between years confuses spatial differences with treatment effects. Selecting only thriving sections further inflates average cover; fix the sampling design before observing which areas appear successful in the field.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「對照監測的生態成效」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","不同年份用不同樣方位置會把空間差異當成工程效果。","河段平均剪力就是每一處岸坡承受的最大剪力"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Moving quadrats between years confuses spatial differences with treatment effects.","Reach average shear is the maximum stress at every bank location"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同年份用不同樣方位置會把空間差異當成工程效果。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Moving quadrats between years confuses spatial differences with treatment effects. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
